### Caching Strategies Demo — API requests
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains' built-in HTTP Client.
### Click "Send Request" above any block below (or run all of them top to bottom).
### App must be running first: npm start

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Baseline (no caching)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### List all products straight from MongoDB
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Reseed the sample catalog (p1..p5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/seed

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Reading strategies — GET, one read per call, no side effects.
### Run the same request twice in a row: first is a MISS, second is a HIT.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Cache-Aside — read p1 (default id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache-aside

### Cache-Aside — read a specific id
GET {{baseUrl}}/cache-aside?id=p1

### Read-Through — read p2 (default id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/read-through

### Read-Through — read a specific id
GET {{baseUrl}}/read-through?id=p1

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Cache clearing — separate from reading, since it's a mutation.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Clear one strategy's key for one id (guarantees the next read above is a MISS)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cache?strategy=cacheAside&id=p1

### Clear every key for one strategy
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cache?strategy=readThrough

### Clear every demo cache key across all strategies
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cache

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Writing strategies — POST, each call runs the full create -> update
### (Write-Back also flushes) story and returns a step-by-step trace.
### Body is optional; omit "id" to auto-generate a fresh product each run.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Write-Through — auto-generated product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-through

### Write-Through — specific product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-through
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "p20",
  "name": "Laptop Stand",
  "category": "Office",
  "price": 29.99,
  "stock": 100
}

### Write-Around — auto-generated product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-around

### Write-Around — specific product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-around
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "p21",
  "name": "Desk Lamp",
  "category": "Office",
  "price": 18.50,
  "stock": 75
}

### Write-Back — auto-generated product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-back

### Write-Back — specific product
POST {{baseUrl}}/write-back
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "p596",
  "name": "New One",
  "category": "Office",
  "price": 42.00,
  "stock": 40
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------
### Inspection helpers — look at raw MongoDB / Redis state for an id.
### Swap ":id" or "p1" below for a productId from any response above.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------

### Raw MongoDB document
GET {{baseUrl}}/inspect/mongo/p1

### Raw Redis entry (strategy: cacheAside, readThrough, writeThrough, writeAround, writeBack)
GET {{baseUrl}}/inspect/redis/p1?strategy=cacheAside
